1.15 Deep Learning Analytics for different types of datasources - text, PSUtils OS Scheduler analytics - ThoughtNet Reinforcement Learning, Recommender Systems, LSTM/GRU Recurrent Neural Networks, Convolution Networks, BackPropagation, Multilayer perceptrons, Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks (KAN) 1.16 Computational Learning Theory Analytics - Complement Diophantines Learning, PAC Learning from numeric and binary encoded datasets 1.17 Time Series Analysis for different types of datasources (music, traffic-electronic and transport, meteorology-precipitation, medical imagery-ECG, financial-stock and commodities price fluctuations) - Multifractal Detrended Fluctuation Analysis (MFDFA) of Music-Financial-Climate(Precipitation) timeseries, SINDy-Sparse Identification of Non-Linear Dynamics model for governing equation discovery (Lorenz, Polynomial) in Financial-Climate(Precipitation) timeseries, Higuchi Fractal Dimension of timeseries data in the context of ( ) verifying Riemann Hypothesis by termination of Matiyasevich Python programs - Loop termination analysis by (1) AI models (2) SINDy governing equations discovery for while loop LHS-RHS ratio series and (3) Logistic map upperbounds for while loop by SINDy Lorenz model and Logistic map (4) Jacob ladder real random walk and longest repeated substring within binary random walk over while loop LHS-RHS ratio - majority of the AI models predict the while loop to be infinite with high probability due to exponential growth of RHS in loop inequality - Infinite loop in Matiyasevich program implies Riemann Hypothesis is True - Link to paper: The Riemann Hypothesis in computer science - [Yu. Matiyasevich] - https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304397519304633 ( ) volatility of stockquote tickers-higher the fractal dimension more unpredictable is the stock (*) Urban sprawls-Fractal dimensions of US Cities as an estimate of area- https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Guoqiang-Shen-2/publication/220649779_Fractal_Dimension_and_Fractal_Growth_of_Urbanized_Areas/links/573df0c208ae9f741b2ffdb6/Fractal-Dimension-and-Fractal-Growth-of-Urbanized-Areas.pdf- "....This observation implies that fractal dimension alone is a fair indicator of the total of urbanized areas but not a good measure of urban population density....", Multimodal Gaussian Mixture Models(GMM) and Gaussian Ensemble Timeseries Forecast of Precipitation by choosing most probable Integer Partition (modes of GMM forecast timeseries correspond to peaks in N-Body gravity), Least Squares Curve fit, Leaky Bucket, ARMA and ARIMA, miscellaneous statistics functions based on R and PythonR (Economic merit - Poverty alleviation example by timeseries correlation of poverty and financial deepening - https://www.researchgate.net/publication/287580802_Financial_development_and_poverty_alleviation_Time_series_evidence_from_Pakistan , Granger causality). Phenomenon known as Gaussian Multiplicative Chaos (GMC) has been found across broad spectrum of disciplines including Quantum Gravity, Financial timeseries, Prime number distribution among others - https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/mathematicians-crack-a-fractal-conjecture-on-chaos/ and section 5 of https://projecteuclid.org/journals/probability-surveys/volume-11/issue-none/Gaussian-multiplicative-chaos-and-applications-A-review/10.1214/13-PS218.pdf on volatility measure in financial markets that is formulated as Gaussian Multiplicative Chaos by raising volatility function to an exponential and simulation of S&P500 returns by Black-Scholes formula, Markov Randomwalks. Ratio timeseries of LHS-RHS of while loop in Matiyasevich python program for Riemann Hypothesis which has been already studied in relation to Logistic maps,if proved to be under Gaussian Multiplicative Chaos Regime,could add to mounting repertoire of evidences on disorder within prime distribution. 1.18 Fame-Merit Equilibrium(any Semantic Network) - applies to all previous merit measures and how they relate to perceptions. Google PageRank is a perception (Fame) ranking based on majority voting while Microsoft Bing SPTAG is an Intrinsic Merit algorithm to find nearest neighbours (URLs) of a search query and rank them by distance. In the absence of 100% good intrinsic merit function, it is often infeasible to ascertain merit exactly. But Market Equilibrium Pricing in algorithmic economics solves this problem approximately by finding an equilibrium point between intrinsic and perceived price of a commodity. Similar Intrinsic(Merit) Versus Perceived(Fame) equilibria can be defined for every class of merit above and solution is only approximate. [Conjecture: Fame-Merit equilibrium and Converging Markov Random Walk (PageRank) rankings should coincide - Both are two facets of mistake-minimizing Nash equilibrium per Condorcet Jury Theorem for infinite jury though algorithmically different - former is a convex program and latter is a markov chain. Convex Optimization has been shown to be solved by Random Walks - https://www.mit.edu/~dbertsim/papers/Optimization/Solving%20Convex%20Programs%20by%20Random%20Walks.pdf . As an evidence for Fame-Merit equilibrium, rarest of rare near-concurrence of Google PageRank and Bing Ranking Factor search result rankings have been captured at https://github.com/shrinivaasanka/asfer-github-code/blob/master/python-src/testlogs/GoogleSearch_bigdatalinuxkernelcloudmachinelearning_22December2023.pdf and https://github.com/shrinivaasanka/asfer-github-code/blob/master/python-src/testlogs/MicrosoftBingSearch_bigdatalinuxkernelcloudmachinelearning_22December2023.pdf - for same query "big data machine learning linux kernel cloud" on 22/12/2023]. NeuronRain implements a faster approximation of asymptotic part of Condorcet Jury Theorem for homogeneous voters of p-bias close to 0.5 which is faster than iterative version requiring factorial calculations in each term.
