    {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shrinivaasanka/asfer-github-code/commits/b03a058c9363db9a3b3c247b96cdcd12dcf9967c",
      "sha": "b03a058c9363db9a3b3c247b96cdcd12dcf9967c",
      "node_id": "MDY6Q29tbWl0MzY5NDUyNzI6YjAzYTA1OGM5MzYzZGI5YTNiM2MyNDdiOTZjZGNkMTJkY2Y5OTY3Yw==",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/shrinivaasanka/asfer-github-code/commit/b03a058c9363db9a3b3c247b96cdcd12dcf9967c",
      "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shrinivaasanka/asfer-github-code/commits/b03a058c9363db9a3b3c247b96cdcd12dcf9967c/comments",
      "commit": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shrinivaasanka/asfer-github-code/git/commits/b03a058c9363db9a3b3c247b96cdcd12dcf9967c",
        "author": {
          "date": "2024-08-01T13:11:32.000+05:30",
          "name": "Srinivasan Kannan",
          "email": "ka.shrinivaasan@gmail.com"
        },
        "committer": {
          "date": "2024-08-01T13:11:32.000+05:30",
          "name": "Srinivasan Kannan",
          "email": "ka.shrinivaasan@gmail.com"
        },
        "message": "-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1534. (JIRA,THEORY and FEATURE) People Analytics - Social Network Analysis - Name paradox implementation generalized to Attribute paradox - related to 14,365,626,711,727,753,876,1127,1128,1129,1130,1204,1263,1269,1427,1442,1452,1534 and all sections on People Analytics, Intrinsic Merit Versus Fame Equilibrium, BKS Conjecture, Stability and Noise Sensitivity of Interview LTF/PTF,Peres Theorem,Unique Identification,Talent Analytics,HR Analytics and Automated Recruitment,Question-Answering,Majority Voting,Condorcet Jury Theorem Variants,Margulis-Ruzzo Thresholds,Novelty Detection,Recommender Systems,AI Question-Answering, Partial Ordered Ranking, Fame-Merit equilibrium, Intrinsic Merit as Query Complexity,Software Analytics-Mythical Manmonth-CathedralAndBazaar,Birthday Paradox - 1 August 2024\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1534.1 python-src/SocialNetworkAnalysis_PeopleAnalytics.py has been updated to change function nameparadox() to attributeparadox() so as to bring all possible people attributes into its fold - attribute name is passed on as additional argument to attributeparadox(). Possible people attributes could be \"Names\",\"Genders\",\"Qualifications\" etc.,:\n    def attributeparadox(self,number_of_attributes=1000,name_of_attribute=\"names\")\n1534.2 Personal Access Token for GitHub codesearch REST API has been updated due to authentication exception:\n    codesearchstats=hranal.codesearch_statistics(opensourceid=\"shrinivaasanka\",personalaccesstoken=\"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\")\n    codesearchstats1=hranal.codesearch_statistics(query=\"shrinivaasanka+THEORY+and+FEATURE\",personalaccesstoken=\"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\")\n1534.3 Function attributeparadox() is invoked for 2 population attributes - Names and Genders:\n    hranal.attributeparadox(number_of_attributes=100000,name_of_attribute=\"names\")\n    hranal.attributeparadox(number_of_attributes=3,name_of_attribute=\"genders\")\n1534.4 Following are the minimum number of people required for atleast 2 people having same attributes earlier - from python-src/testlogs/SocialNetworkAnalysis_PeopleAnalytics.log.1August2024:\n\tattributeparadox(): number of  names  =  100000\n\tattributeparadox(): Birthday paradox variant for  names  - Minimum number of people required for atleast 2 people having same  names  (k) with atleast 50% probability = 373.33007682967144\n\tattributeparadox(): number of  genders  =  3\n\tattributeparadox(): Birthday paradox variant for  genders  - Minimum number of people required for atleast 2 people having same  genders  (k) with atleast 50% probability = 3.099734050626334\n1534.5 This update resolves JIRA issue https://krishnairesearch.atlassian.net/browse/NEUR-43",
